    "content": "Overview Coffee is predominantly cultivated in mountainous environments, where slopes create unique visual challenges in high-resolution imagery. The same coffee system can appear strikingly different depending on the slope effect and the angle of the shadows cast by the terrain. These slope artifacts can distort the perception of planting patterns, tree density, or canopy structure, making it difficult to accurately interpret or classify coffee systems.\nExamples idlatlontopiccoffee planting patternshade planting patternshade levelagepruningvarietyintercropirrigationspecial patternslope artifactimagery datestreetview linkgoogle earth linkgoogle maps linkcountry Steep slopes create artifacts that are sometime hard to interpret. Both coffee plots are planted following the same pattern, but shadows due to the slope drastically change the way they look. 19 11.91844904 107.9358602 Slop artifact Regular Full sun Mature Infrequent Robusta Bare soil / weeding No visible irrigation pattern Normal Yes 12/27/23 View in Google Earth View in Google MapsVietnam This is a coffee plot with intercropped productive trees. The coffee trees appear large, possibly indicating infrequent pruning. 29 21.41708386 103.6692318 Slop artifact Regular Regular Medium Mature Frequent Arabica Bare soil / weeding No visible irrigation pattern Normal Yes 11/17/23 View in Google Earth View in Google MapsVietnam Dense agroforestry systems grown on steep terrain. The difference of colors between the two plots is likely due to different illumination resulting from the terrain effect. 43 13.834786 -89.81061 Slop artifact Regular Irregular Full sun Mature Frequent Unknown Bare soil / weeding No visible irrigation pattern Normal Yes 5/4/23 View in Google Earth View in Google MapsEl Salvador Densely planted coffee grown on steep terrain. The difference of colors between the two plots is likely due to different illumination resulting from the terrain effect. 44 13.840746 -89.79725 Slop artifact Regular Regular Full sun Mature Frequent Unknown Bare soil / weeding No visible irrigation pattern Normal Yes 5/4/23 View in Google Earth View in Google MapsEl Salvador Full sun robusta coffee. The trees are infrequently pruned and are larger than what can be seen in Latin America. 91 11.4523853 107.7829299 Slop artifact Regular Full sun Mature Frequent Robusta Bare soil / weeding No visible irrigation pattern Normal Yes 2/22/24 View in Google Earth View in Google MapsVietnam",
