    "content": "Cocoa trees are medium-sized, with mature heights typically ranging from four to eight meters, though some trees may grow as tall as twelve meters in favorable conditions. The tree has large, leathery leaves that are arranged alternately in a flat, two-row (distichous) pattern along the branches. The leaves are oval to elliptical in shape, measuring between 12 and 60 cm in length and between 4 and 20 cm in width. Leaf tips are pointed, and the bases are usually rounded or heart-shaped.\nOne of the most distinctive visual features is the color of young leaves, or flushes, which emerge reddish-pink before gradually turning light green as they mature.\nA few samples idlatlontopiccocoa planting patternshade planting patternshade levelagepruningplot boundariesintercropspecial patternimagery datestreetview linkgoogle earth linkgoogle maps link Ghana 29 6.69890334 -2.23953014 Plot boundaries Irregular Irregular Low Mature Infrequent Unclear Bare soil / weeding Normal 4/23/21 View in Google Earth View in Google Maps Ghana 30 6.777395 -2.185375 Plot boundaries Irregular Irregular Low Mature Infrequent Unclear Bare soil / weeding Normal 4/23/21 View in Google Earth View in Google Maps Ghana 31 6.63949689 -2.47133791 Plot boundaries Irregular Irregular Low Mature Infrequent Unclear Bare soil / weeding Normal 12/12/15 View in Google Earth View in Google Maps Ghana 32 6.53212462 -2.47905344 Plot boundaries Irregular Irregular Low Mature Infrequent Unclear Bare soil / weeding Normal 2/12/18 View in Google Earth View in Google Maps Ghana 34 6.8310052 -2.2880488 Cocoa planting pattern Irregular Irregular Full sun Mature Frequent Unclear No weeding Normal 12/24/24 View in Google Earth View in Google Maps Vietnam 43 11.37652552 107.3698343 Shade level Irregular Regular Medium Mature Infrequent Unclear Cover crop Normal 1/22/24 View in Street View View in Google Earth View in Google Maps",
